# palette — overview

The palette is the one set of WASM build/runtime tooling. Each runtime is a pinned prebuilt (or build recipe) that runs untrusted source in the capability-gated sandbox — no OS process, no host access beyond a granted preopen.

app :palette__overview do
  title       "palette — overview"
  description "The palette is the one set of WASM build/runtime tooling."
end

## Build the runtimes (from the committed pinned specs)

### build + register every runtime in the set
```bash
  work kit build palette
```

### or just one
```bash
  work kit build palette python
```

## Run source in the sandbox

```bash
  qjs    /w/app.js
  python /w/app.py
  ruby   /w/app.rb
```

Each runtime's own resources (stdlib) preopen automatically; grant the script's dir as an extra preopen.